# Project Charter
## Logistics Shipment Tracking System

### 1. Project Overview
This project aims to develop a centralized shipment tracking system that allows customers and internal operational teams to monitor shipment status throughout the delivery process.

### 2. Business Problem
The existing shipment tracking process may involve fragmented information, manual status updates, and limited shipment visibility for customers.

### 3. Project Objectives
- Improve shipment visibility.
- Provide real-time or timely shipment status updates.
- Reduce customer inquiries related to shipment status.
- Improve operational monitoring and efficiency.

### 4. Project Scope

**In Scope**
- Shipment tracking by tracking number.
- Shipment status monitoring.
- Delivery status updates.
- Customer tracking interface.
- Internal operational monitoring.

**Out of Scope**
- Payment gateway integration.
- Warehouse inventory management.
- Route optimization.

### 5. Key Stakeholders
- Project Sponsor
- IT Project Manager
- Business Analyst
- System Analyst
- Development Team
- Operations Team
- Customer Service Team
- Customers

### 6. Expected Deliverables
- Business Requirement Document (BRD)
- Functional Requirement Specification (FRS)
- Business Process Flow
- System Architecture
- Project Plan
- Testing Documentation

### 7. Success Criteria
- Customers can check shipment status using a tracking number.
- Internal teams can monitor shipment progress.
- Shipment information is consistently updated.
- Customer inquiries related to tracking are reduced.

### 8. Project Assumptions
This is a simulated portfolio project. All business scenarios and requirements are fictional and created for demonstration purposes.
